FACILITYOS
----------

I read the parcel page plus the surrounding LogisticsOS product pages (chain of custody, package tracking, inbound logistics, digital mailroom, high-density folders, interoffice shipping, check-in/out, asset auditing, EOL, SKU-level tracking, PO line-item receiving) and the AI/locker/integration blog posts, then checked each candidate gap against our own code rather than against memory.

Where they have something we genuinely don't

Jeg kiggede på FaciliyOS for se om de havde features som vi manglede, som vi evt. kunne implementerer. Der er 12:

1. Locker vendor integrations. They integrate with ten locker vendors (TZ SMArt, Luxer One, MyPup, Smiota, Parcel Pending, Variocube, StrongPoint, Hublok, Gantner, Metra): drop in locker → auto-notification with locker location + PIN/QR → 24/7 self-pickup → signature optional. This is the single biggest gap — the product is scoped in Operia but not built.

2. Recipient self-service. They have kiosks (touchscreen: check if my package arrived, schedule pickup) and phone-barcode self-pickup from high-density folders. Operia has no receiver-facing surface at all — final receivers get a notification and that's the end of their access.

3. Carrier integrations. UPS/FedEx/USPS visibility on inbound volume, and the USPS Delivery Partner Program auto-generating arrival notifications. Our carriers table is app-owned master data (a name list) — no carrier API, no tracking-number lookup against a carrier.

4. PO line-item receiving / ERP reconciliation. Pull the PO from the ERP, match received items to line items, verify/edit quantities, flag discrepancies, generate a receipt manifest, close the PO. We have zero purchase-order concept and no ERP connector. Distinct product line, not a feature tweak.

5. Depth in inventory (SKU-level tracking). They do lots, expiry/use-by dates, FIFO, bin/shelf/aisle-level locations, bulk pick-pack-stage requests, and physical audits with instant reconciliation. Our inventory_items is flat — sku, quantity, reorder_point, unit, unit_cost, on_order — with handheld goods-in/goods-out/count on the quantity only. No lots, no expiry, no bin level, no movement journal.

6. Approval workflows ("Advanced Mode"). Asset movements, ownership changes and retirement requests route to a designated reviewer who approves/declines, with notifications. Grep finds no approval concept anywhere in our migrations. For regulated/government buyers this is usually a hard requirement.

7. Structured end-of-life. Retirement reason + disposition method (recycled / donated / sold / auctioned / disposed) + surplus reporting for finance. We have retired and written_off statuses and nothing else — no disposition capture, no surplus report.

8. Asset audit / stocktake campaigns. A scan-to-verify pass that updates location, records condition + photo, and produces a reconciliation report. We have asset_events and condition capture, but no audit run as a workflow.

9. Maintenance-due and CapEx tracking. They flag high-expenditure assets and track maintenance due dates / approaching retirement. We store purchased_at, purchase_price, warranty_until — but no maintenance schedule and no CapEx flag.

10. Mail sorter hardware (OPEX, Fluence) and outbound shipping via 2Ship — batch load-and-scan sorters, and a consolidated multi-carrier shipping history with cost analysis.

11. Scheduled report delivery + Excel export. They advertise automated report delivery to leadership. Ours renders PDF/Word/CSV on demand only; there is no scheduler and no .xlsx.

12. High-density barcode mail folders — barcoded folders in bins replacing physical mailboxes, reusable on clear. A physical-process product we have no analogue for.

13. Platform breadth. FacilityOS bundles VisitorOS, ContractorOS and EmergencyOS around the same facility buyer. Not parcel features, but it's what they sell against.


Where they don't reach us

Worth knowing, because most of these are structural rather than catch-up-able in a sprint:

Der er også nogle punkter Operia allerede har, som FacilityOS mangler:

- GDPR/NIS2 layer. SAR export, retention schedules with purge, anonymize-instead-of-delete RPCs, ROPA, breach register, free-text field register, DPA/subprocessor docs, AI disclosure gate, read-audit, immutable parcel_events. Their pages say essentially nothing beyond "secure audit trails" — they're a US product.
- Booking (rooms/vehicles/equipment) — no equivalent on their side.
- Route planning with real map providers (ORS + Google).
- Employee directory as system of record: Entra ID Graph sync plus CSV/SFTP/email import with dry-run preview and import log. They only offer Excel/ServiceNow import, and only for assets.
- White-labeling depth: label designer, home/handheld design editors, notification templates, and per-tenant text overrides on i18n keys.
- Multi-tenant platform layer: product/feature entitlements with expiry, impersonation, billing, per-company login-security policy, passkeys/biometrics.
- NFC/MIFARE card handover, handling classes, proxy collection, "left at location" rules.
- Danish-first localisation. For the DK/EU market this is not a small thing.



